      "body": "## Motivation\n\n#44455 routes the bf16 `lm_head` through aiter `tgemm` on gfx1250. On gfx950 the same path also beats `torch.matmul` (hipBLASLt heuristic) at decode/verify batch sizes, e.g. for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (vocab 248320, hidden 2560).\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdd `SGLANG_OPT_AITER_LM_HEAD_GEMM` (default off). With `SGLANG_USE_AITER=1` it enables the existing aiter lm_head path on any HIP arch; gfx1250 keeps it on unconditionally.\n\n## Accuracy\n\nUnchanged: max relative difference vs `torch.matmul` is at bf16 rounding level (≤3e-3), and MTP accept length is unchanged in serving (3.03–3.05 vs 3.02–3.04).\n\n## Benchmark (MI355X, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, NEXTN MTP 3 steps / 4 draft tokens, 8k/1k)\n\nLM-head GEMM, [M, 2560] x [2560, 248320]:\n\n| M | torch.matmul | aiter tgemm | Speedup |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 193.2 us | 187.1 us | +3% |\n| 16 | 204.8 us | 192.8 us | +6% |\n| 32 | 222.4 us | 194.3 us | +13% |\n| 64 | 283.8 us | 202.1 us | +29% |\n| 128 | 277.9 us | 278.7 us | 0% |\n\nEnd to end (2 repeats, measured acceptance):\n\n| | Output tok/s | Median TPOT | P90 interactivity |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| C16 | +4.6% | −4.3% | +4.5% |\n| C12 | +1.3% | −2.8% | +4.5% |\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41667075435](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41667075435)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41667075233](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41667075233)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41667075656](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41667075656)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests